verilator (5.054+git202611072109.74cf7aa-1+nvcx2) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  * d/patches: only the force/release fix nvcx's XPMs need (Vivado's
    xpm_cdc with INIT_SYNC_FF=1 forces and releases whole unpacked arrays):
    force-whole-unpacked-arrays.patch now has V3Slice split every force,
    release, assign and deassign of an unpacked array into elements, as
    forwarded upstream (verilator/verilator#9091, issue #9090); a force or
    assign of a whole array from a queue or a streaming expression is
    "Unsupported:" rather than an internal error. Dropped
    force-range-bitsel-reads.patch, force-struct-array-ranges-unsupported.patch,
    forceable-procedural-assign.patch and
    force-arrays-in-structs-unsupported.patch.

 -- Graeme Smecher <gsmecher@t0.technology>  Sun, 08 Nov 2026 12:00:00 -0700

verilator (5.054+git202611072109.74cf7aa-1+nvcx1) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  * Upstream snapshot 74cf7aada (master, 2026-11-07), which has nvcx's fix
    for wide unpacked array copies between opposite directions (#9075).
  * d/patches: the force/release series refreshed against it, in the order
    of its pull requests: force-whole-unpacked-arrays.patch,
    force-range-bitsel-reads.patch, force-struct-array-ranges-unsupported.patch,
    forceable-procedural-assign.patch (new: a procedural assign of a
    /*verilator forceable*/ signal), force-arrays-in-structs-unsupported.patch.
  * d/patches/sched-sense-net-init.patch: fire change sensitivities on
    continuously assigned nets at time 0, as xsim does (Xilinx XPM
    xpm_fifo_axis depends on it). Not forwarded: upstream chose otherwise in
    #8911; nvcx runs Verilator cores alongside xsim.
  * d/patches/tristate-z-tested-input.patch: refreshed.
  * d/rules: NVCX_TESTS runs those patches' tests.
  * The upstream version of a snapshot names its commit's UTC date and time,
    so that two snapshots of one day sort in order.

