verilator (5.054+git20261107.acdc8dc-1+nvcx1) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  * Upstream snapshot acdc8dc72 (master, 2026-11-07), which nvcx carries
    with its own fixes until they are released. The upstream source is now
    the tag or commit in upstream.ref (build-deb.sh).
  * Drop d/patches/const-net-change-sensitivity.patch: fixed upstream in
    61ff77472 (#8911), whose t_sched_sense_const covers what our tests did.
  * d/patches/force-whole-unpacked-arrays.patch: force/release of a whole
    unpacked array or a slice (Xilinx XPM CDC models' GSR emulation) no
    longer fails with an internal error in V3Force.
  * d/patches/force-struct-array-ranges-unsupported.patch,
    force-arrays-in-structs-unsupported.patch: report as unsupported the
    forces whose element numbering is ambiguous, instead of simulating them
    wrongly or not at all.
  * d/patches/force-range-bitsel-reads.patch: element reads within a forced
    range after a bit select force on one of its elements.
  * d/rules: NVCX_TESTS runs those patches' tests and t_sched_sense_const.

 -- Graeme Smecher <gsmecher@t0.technology>  Sat, 07 Nov 2026 08:40:00 -0700

verilator (5.054-1+nvcx1) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  * New upstream release 5.054, packaged for nvcx (contrib/verilator) from
    Debian's 5.048-1 packaging.
  * d/rules: name the build through VERILATOR_SRC_VERSION (src/config_rev
    no longer carries UNKNOWN_REV); honour nodoc; drop the config_rev save;
    run the regression tests our patches add (NVCX_TESTS).
  * d/control: the documentation's build dependencies under <!nodoc>;
    depend on make, which --build and --binary run.
  * d/patches/tristate-z-tested-input.patch: accept an input-only submodule
    port that is only tested for Z (UNISIM DSP48E2, RAMB18E2), rather than
    refusing it as "tristate in top-level IO". A prototype, not forwarded.
  * d/patches/const-net-change-sensitivity.patch: with --timing, fire a
    change sensitivity on a constant-assigned net once at time 0, as without
    --timing (a regression from upstream 5a410e95a, #8911; UNISIM RAMB18E2
    read back wrong data). Not yet forwarded.

